Is displeasure the same as anger?  Yes.  (Though I point out that the
source painfully uses "angry" to describe both divine anger and negative
alignment.)

Since you're a wererat you can easily get some corpses of former pets.
If you still have a cross-aligned altar, you could mollify your god that 
way.  You'll have to do it twice: your god is twice angry now that 
you've prayed while he was angry already.

You'll take a small alignment hit from those sacrifices, and a rather 
large one if you kill them yourself, so don't try to convert any altars.
Instead, go back to a co-aligned altar, and do any old sacrifice to
check and make sure that it is safe.  Then pray.

If you lack a cross-aligned altar, your only hope is to carry on until 
you find a cure, or something big and mean enough to mollify your god 
the old-fashioned way.  Luckily your balrog can take care of you.

